The raw Global Superstore Orders table (51,000+ rows) was messy: missing values, inconsistent formats and no structure a decision-maker could trust. So before any chart was drawn, the data itself was fixed first.
The table went through a complete 9-step Excel cleaning process: missing-value checks (Postal Code gaps were kept honestly missing, not faked), a duplicate-row scan, TRIM/CLEAN plus non-breaking-space removal, data-type standardization, date logic validation (Ship Date never before Order Date), value validations (Quantity, Sales, and Shipping Cost above zero), categorical validation, and relationship checks against the Returns and People tables. The table grew from 24 to 26 columns with new analytical columns Shipping Days, Profit Margin, Profit Status, Return Status, and Year/Month/Quarter turning raw records into analysis-ready data.
On that clean foundation, a 4-page Power BI dashboard was built. The Executive Overview answers the biggest question first: $12.6M in total sales and $1.5M in total profit. Regional & Manager Performance shows which regions and managers are actually driving those numbers. Product & Customer Analytics breaks down which products and customers matter most. And Returns & Risk Analysis closes the loop honestly 1,080+ returned orders at a 4.19% return rate, showing exactly where revenue leaks and which patterns need attention.
Built with Power BI, DAX, and Power Query, this dashboard is proof of the full pipeline: cleaning messy data, modelling it properly and turning it into visuals a business can act on not just look at.
